{
    "background_story": "Major was a proud and powerful stallion with a gleaming black coat. As a showjumper, he was known for his impressive technique and precision. One day, while competing in a high-stakes tournament, Major suffered a severe injury to his dorsal muscles, which run along his spine. Devastated, his owner and trainer, Emma, feared that his jumping days were over. However, with intense rehabilitation and care, Major slowly regained his strength. Emma worked with him to redevelop his muscles, focusing on exercises that targeted his dorsal region. After months of hard work, Major made a triumphant return to the competition arena, his dorsal muscles stronger than ever. His remarkable recovery was a testament to the power of perseverance and the unbreakable bond between Emma and her loyal steed.",
